# Call-site ledger of flit-core at eeaf9e783c87c331f1d73bb2f5553fc79016aae1.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in flit-core.md.
#
# Receivers and values used below (flit-core.md, "Values"):
#   public: only the PEP 517 hooks of flit_core.buildapi and the command line
#     python -m flit_core.wheel (flit_core/README.rst; doc/bootstrap.rst);
#     every other function is private (J1) and gets what the package passes.
#   the TOML document: dicts, lists, strs, ints, floats, bools and datetime
#     values that tomllib.loads or the vendored tomli makes; a call on such a
#     value is named by the type that has the method (only a dict has get).
#   paths: Path('pyproject.toml'), Path.cwd(), Path(<directory>) and what is
#     derived from them: a pathlib.PosixPath on Linux, a pathlib.WindowsPath
#     on Windows (CI: ubuntu-latest and windows-latest).
#   text streams: the io.TextIOWrapper of open(..., 'w'), the io.StringIO of
#     WheelBuilder._write_to_zip and of SdistBuilder.build.
default reject flit_core.common.VCSError.__str__: flit_core never makes a VCSError (no package code raises or builds one; flit, the command-line tool, does), so no formatted or str()-converted value is one
default reject flit_core.config.EntryPointsConflict.__str__: no formatted or str()-converted value is an EntryPointsConflict: its only raise (LoadedConfig.add_scripts, 236:23) propagates to the caller, and the only exceptions that the package formats are the ValueError of email.headerregistry.Address (pep621_people) and the ConfigError or ValueError of _license_files_from_globs, whose args[0] (a str) it formats

